{%- comment -%}
  The other policies, listed at the foot of a policy page.

  Shopify renders shop policies with its own fixed markup and ignores theme
  templates entirely — templates/policy.json is rejected outright ("Template
  type 'policy' does not support JSON templates") and templates/policy.liquid
  is never reached. So the page itself cannot be rebuilt; it can only be styled,
  and anything extra has to be added around it from the layout.

  This is that extra: the set of policies, minus the one being read, so someone
  who has just read about returns can get to shipping without going back to the
  footer. Built from the shop's own policies, so it follows whatever is turned
  on in Settings.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign shown = 0 -%}
{%- for policy in shop.policies -%}
  {%- if policy.title != page_title and policy.body != blank -%}
    {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- if shown > 0 -%}
  <nav class="policy-also" aria-label="Other policies">
    {%- comment -%}
      A literal rather than a translation key: a missing key renders as
      "Translation missing: …" rather than as blank, so `default` never fires.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="policy-also__label">Also worth reading</span>
    {%- for policy in shop.policies -%}
      {%- if policy.title != page_title and policy.body != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ policy.url }}">{{ policy.title }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </nav>
{%- endif -%}
